From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: qcom: describe MSM8226 display SMMU

The first native boot bound MDP and DSI but KMS stopped with ENODEV
from msm_kms_init_vm because no display IOMMU was described. Add the
MSM8226 display SMMUv1 at fd928000 using vendor IRQ73 and context IRQ47,
and map the non-secure MDP stream0. Keep disabled in the common DT until
a board opts into native display. Reuse the existing MSM8226 context-bank
offset and SCTLR quirks.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g-native.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g-native.dts
index b7b7adcfb..08da49bf4 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g-native.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g-native.dts
@@ -6,6 +6,14 @@ &framebuffer0 {
 	status = "disabled";
 };
 
+&mdp_smmu {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&mdss_mdp {
+	iommus = <&mdp_smmu 0>;
+};
+
 &mdss {
 	status = "okay";
 };
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226.dtsi b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226.dtsi
index bcf14a3b1..61bb37145 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226.dtsi
@@ -1150,6 +1150,21 @@ mmcc: clock-controller@fd8c0000 {
 				      "dsi0pllbyte";
 		};
 
+		mdp_smmu: iommu@fd928000 {
+			compatible = "qcom,msm8226-smmu", "arm,smmu-v1";
+			reg = <0xfd928000 0x10000>;
+			#iommu-cells = <1>;
+			#global-interrupts = <1>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 73 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 47 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 47 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 47 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			clocks = <&mmcc MDSS_AHB_CLK>, <&mmcc MDSS_AXI_CLK>;
+			clock-names = "iface", "bus";
+			power-domains = <&mmcc MDSS_GDSC>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		mdss: display-subsystem@fd900000 {
 			compatible = "qcom,mdss";
 			reg = <0xfd900000 0x100>, <0xfd924000 0x1000>;
